### 2) Who are the top 10% of customers by Customer Lifetime Value (CLV)? Why it's valuable: Identifies VIP customers. Businesses can use this list to offer loyalty rewards, exclusive early access to new releases, or specialized support to retain their most valuable users.

#### SQL SOLUTION:

WITH CustomerSpending AS (
    SELECT 
        c.CustomerId, 
        c.FirstName, 
        c.LastName,
        c.email,
        SUM(i.Total) AS TotalSpend
    FROM invoices i
    JOIN customers c ON i.customerId = c.customerId
    GROUP BY c.CustomerId, c.FirstName, c.LastName
),
CustomerBuckets AS (
    SELECT *,
           NTILE(10) OVER(ORDER BY TotalSpend DESC) as bucket_alias
    FROM CustomerSpending
    -- Removed the extra GROUP BY here
)
SELECT 
    FirstName, 
    LastName,
    Email,
    TotalSpend,
    RANK() OVER(ORDER BY TotalSpend DESC) as vip_rank
FROM CustomerBuckets
WHERE bucket_alias = 1
ORDER BY TotalSpend DESC;

